        "original_id": "ad772af3-7c0d-53bf-9ee3-ab9bc6236371",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Æthelweard, Æthelred I of Wessex, Alfred the Great, Cynric\n- Works: Anglo-Saxon Chronicle, Chronicon Æthelweardi\n- Roles: ealdorman, historian\n- Concepts: Anglo-Saxon annals, Old English, Latin versions\n\nFacts:\n- The Anglo-Saxon Chronicle is a collection of annals in Old English that chronicles the history of the Anglo-Saxons.\n- Everything known about Cynric comes from the Anglo-Saxon Chronicle.\n- Æthelweard, also called Ethelward, died around 998 and was descended from Æthelred I of Wessex, the elder brother of Alfred the Great.\n- Æthelweard was an ealdorman and the author of a Latin version of the Anglo-Saxon Chronicle called the Chronicon Æthelweardi.",
